# Without this the build context was 275 MB: 138 MB of build/, 73 MB of
# .dart_tool/ and 18 MB of .git, all uploaded to the daemon and COPYed into the
# image on every build.
#
# It was not only slow, it was wrong. `flutter pub get` runs before `COPY . .`
# so the dependency layer can cache — but the COPY then overwrote the
# container's freshly-resolved .dart_tool with the HOST's, which is generated by
# a different Flutter (nix 3.44.4) than the image builds with (3.44.0). A stale
# toolchain artifact was leaking into the build.
#
# And since build/ and .dart_tool/ change on every local `flutter build`, that
# COPY layer was invalidated every single time, so the cached dependency layer
# below it could never actually be reused.

# Build outputs
build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# VCS and local tooling
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Docs and deploy configs that have no business in the image
*.md
Caddyfile*
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Tests and dev-only tooling. The image ships the app; CI runs the tests.
test/
tool/
coverage/
